From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8450: add the bandwidth monitors

SM8450 has the two BWMONs mainline describes for SM8550: the CPU to LLCC
monitor (BWMON v4) at 0x190b6400 and the LLCC to DDR one (v5) at
0x19091000, at the same interrupts. Qualcomm's tree has both (qcom,bwmon4
and qcom,bwmon5). Without them nothing votes the CPU's memory bandwidth:
once the interconnects' sync_state drops the boot votes, DDR stays at the
display's vote and the CPUs stall on memory. On the AYANEO Pocket VERT the
Steam UI lagged and a game never reached its menu.

The OPP steps are the stock DDR (547-3196 MHz, 4-byte bus) and LLCC
(300-1066 MHz, 16-byte bus) tables. The sm8450 compatibles are not in the
binding yet; the driver matches the fallbacks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
@@ -5288,6 +5288,86 @@
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		pmu@19091000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,sm8450-llcc-bwmon", "qcom,sc7280-llcc-bwmon";
+			reg = <0 0x19091000 0 0x1000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 81 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interconnects = <&mc_virt MASTER_LLCC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY
+					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>;
+
+			operating-points-v2 = <&llcc_bwmon_opp_table>;
+
+			llcc_bwmon_opp_table: opp-table {
+				compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+				opp-0 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <2188000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-1 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <3072000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-2 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <6220000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-3 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <6832000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-4 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8368000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-5 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <10944000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-6 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <12784000>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+
+		pmu@190b6400 {
+			compatible = "qcom,sm8450-cpu-bwmon", "qcom,sdm845-bwmon";
+			reg = <0 0x190b6400 0 0x600>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 581 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interconnects = <&gem_noc MASTER_APPSS_PROC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY
+					 &gem_noc SLAVE_LLCC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>;
+
+			operating-points-v2 = <&cpu_bwmon_opp_table>;
+
+			cpu_bwmon_opp_table: opp-table {
+				compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+				opp-0 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <4800000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-1 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <7456000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-2 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <9600000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-3 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <12896000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-4 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <14928000>;
+				};
+
+				opp-5 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <17056000>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+
 		gem_noc: interconnect@19100000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,sm8450-gem-noc";
 			reg = <0 0x19100000 0 0xbb800>;
